Parent: 1444

## Context
Author request (2026-11-02), second of the three principles split out of 1444:
document a manual route that an agent can follow without running the helper
script, to preserve useful procedures when automation is unavailable.

## Scope
The manual route describes inputs, decisions, checks, and outputs without
requiring the helper script or newly written code. Keep one procedural
specification that automation implements; explain any limits or extra cost of
the manual route. Preserve authorization and verification requirements.
Demonstrate on one existing scripted workflow (selected by the 1444 inventory).

## Relevant files
- rules/coding-python.md
- skills/harness-doctor/references/authoring-skills.md
- skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md, if present; otherwise locate its maintained source
- rules/workflow.md (diagnosis discipline)
- One existing scripted skill and its helper, selected after inventory

## Exit criteria
- [x] The maintained authoring guidance requires a documented manual route for
      scripted workflows, derived from the same procedural specification the
      automation implements.
      Done: authoring-skills.md § Toolkit principles (310223ae, b5c1383a).
- [ ] The selected workflow's manual route is demonstrated without its helper
      and its outcome compared with automation on the same known input.
- [ ] Run checks appropriate to changed files; regenerate generated guidance
      or catalogs only when their sources change.

## Verification
Bounded procedural walkthrough and reproducible examples for the pilot. Add
behavioral tests only where script behavior changes; do not pin prose with
wording tests or introduce a new enforcement guard merely to police the
principle.
